[Music]  a local educator is navigating students  not just through school but through life  for today's teacher appreciation week  story mary jane belliesa takes us to  mission high where helping students goes  beyond the classroom  it's a one of a kind school with a  one-of-a-kind teacher i've had this  passion for arts and i always had this  kind of dream to take everything that i  learned and take it to a school that  maybe didn't have the same access to the  arts so i actually started volunteering  with a community  program for at-risk youth and that's how  i found mission high school mission high  school supports students who are going  through recovery from substance abuse or  addiction it's a place for second  chances being a teenager is hard no  matter what situation you're in and  seeing that they can feel comfortable  and that you're building relationships  with them and that they trust me really  makes a difference because they've gone  through a lot and dallas johnston knows  she's helping improve lives through her  lessons from bringing  musicians in to do guitar classes  artists to come in and do drawings  spoken word poetry open mic nights  painting sculpting  it's really really cool to see the kids  find a healthy outlet and i'm hoping  that's what i can provide by bringing in  arts integration with over 20 years of  experience johnston is more than just a  teacher principal barbara collins says  she is a rock for her students just to  watch her process how to help them grow  not only as writers but as individuals  that believe in themselves academically  it's so beautiful you can't let one bad  day even one bad week  wipe out all the good you know it's like  you really have to focus on the  difference that you're making the  changes that you can make mary jean  bellassa live local now

